uploads to api.github.com), from the authority that signs for GitHub
now (Sectigo: its two older roots, USERTrust, and its two roots of 2021)
and the one that did before (DigiCert). Each is the certificate of that
name in Mozilla's list of roots as Debian's ca-certificates carries it,
its SHA-256 fingerprint the one its authority publishes (written above
each; check with: openssl x509 -noout -fingerprint -sha256). A server
under another root is not trusted until its root is added here.

